<table>
<caption>Reported annual imports and calculated shares · gross extra-EU flows</caption>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">China-origin tonnes</th><th scope="col">All extra-EU tonnes</th><th scope="col">China mass share</th><th scope="col">China value share</th><th scope="col">Mass HHI bounds</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
$annual_rows
</tbody></table>
</div>
<p>The import share uses matching net tonnes or nominal euros. The bounds on the Herfindahl–Hirschman Index (HHI) follow from China’s share <i>s</i> of import mass. China alone contributes <i>s</i>². If all other mass belonged to one origin, it would add (1 − <i>s</i>)². The interval describes possible origin concentration on a zero-to-one scale. The index measures concentration of this import basket. A disruption assessment also needs production routes and EU demand. <a href="out/comext_audit.json">Eurostat inputs · source update $comext_vintage</a>.</p>

<p>China introduced licensing for specified medium and heavy rare-earth items on 4 April 2025, including covered magnets and powders. EU imports recorded under the broader basket from China fell <strong>$china_decline</strong> in April–September against the same months in 2024. Other origins also fell, by <strong>$other_decline</strong>. The decrease in China-origin arrivals was concentrated later in the window, with July at its lowest and September above its year-earlier level. Full-year China-origin mass rose <strong>$annual_gain</strong>. The comparison describes arrivals. Timing in transit, orders, demand, shifts in product mix and the scope of licensing limit causal interpretation. <a href="$licensing">April licensing notice</a> · <a href="$comext">Eurostat Comext</a> · <a href="$iea">IEA discussion of the 2025 episode</a>.</p>
<p>The Atlas’s earlier filed study compared the same magnet product code with ferrite and found no decline of the size it set out to test. Its early event window, benchmark and origin filters differ from this comparison. The matched-month figures here provide an absolute mass benchmark, while the filed result compares two product series. <a href="../export-controls">Atlas export-controls study</a>.</p>

